<v Daniel>Oh, like their encouragement and active engagement.</v>

78
00:07:59.096 --> 00:08:13.854
<v Maya>Exactly. Tutoring inherently fixes this inequality because, well, the student can't hide in the back of the room. It forces engagement. Right. And remarkably, Bloom actually predicted in that 1984 paper that computer courses, he specifically referenced the early</v>

